src/single-sided-lp/AbstractSingleSidedLP.sol:finalizeAndRedeemWithdrawRequest|class=C15|High|From the same one-legged-request state (or on the canonical config where only the illiquid leg has a registered manager), the escrowed exit path _redeemShares(isEscrowed=true) → _withdrawPendingRequests reverts for every caller — division by zero on w.sharesAmount == 0, or an extcodesize revert calling manager == address(0) — because this function, unlike its siblings hasPendingWithdrawals and tokenizeWithdrawRequest, has neither a zero-manager guard nor a w.requestId != 0 guard, permanently freezing the LP value already handed to the other leg's manager plus the account's escrowed shares.|src/single-sided-lp/AbstractSingleSidedLP.sol|<work>/notional/zone-hunt-out/verify/gates/17_src_single_sided_lp_AbstractSingleSidedLP_sol_finalizeAndRedeemWithdrawRequest/aux.sol
